Lakṣmaṇa seats Sītā and boards Niṣāda boat --- Lakṣmaṇa leaves Sumantra with chariot ashore --- Lakṣmaṇa begs pardon and falls weeping --- Lakṣmaṇa owns Rāma abandons her for slander --- Lakṣmaṇa cites order and longing to leave her at edge --- Lakṣmaṇa names holy hermitage across Jāhnavī --- Lakṣmaṇa commends her to Vālmīki Daśaratha friend --- Lakṣmaṇa bids devotion to Rāma for highest good